From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 23:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pm_runtime: gate ALL callbacks (not just resume) on CIX Sky1

Patch 9011 gated __pm_runtime_resume to prevent the deferred-probe SError.
That fix prevented one crash path but missed another: during system idle,
rpm_suspend -> pm_generic_runtime_suspend -> acpi_subsys_runtime_suspend
calls regmap_read/write on syscon MMIO that is held-in-reset/unclocked.

Crash stack captured on .66 at t=0.596s (7.1.2-ncz2 #1 PREEMPT):
  el1h_64_error_handler
  __regmap_has_tag_bits
  regmap_write
  regmap_bus_read
  __pm_runtime_resume
  rpm_suspend+0xc8
  pm_generic_runtime_suspend+0x68
  acpi_subsys_runtime_suspend+0x20
  rpm_callback+0xa2
  rpm_suspend+0x3c
  __schedule+0x218

Fix: extend the 9011 gate from __pm_runtime_resume to __rpm_callback,
which is the central dispatch for ALL pm callbacks (resume, suspend,
idle). When cix_system_ready is false, skip every callback and return 0
(success) so the rpm core proceeds normally. The device's actual
hardware state is set up later when the system is ready.

__rpm_callback has no 'out' label (only 'fail:'), so return 0 directly
instead of using goto out.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/base/power/runtime.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)
diff --git a/drivers/base/power/runtime.c b/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
index 69d7cdf0a3d9..e74d7e4454f8 100644
--- a/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/runtime.c
@@ -397,6 +397,23 @@ static int __rpm_callback(int (*cb)(struct device *), struct device *dev)
 	int retval = 0, idx;
 	bool use_links = dev->power.links_count > 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * NCZ CIX Sky1 boot fix (patch 9012): skip ALL runtime PM callbacks
+	 * (resume AND suspend) until late_initcall sets cix_system_ready.
+	 *
+	 * Patch 9011 only gated __pm_runtime_resume, but the crash also
+	 * occurs via rpm_suspend -> acpi_subsys_runtime_suspend ->
+	 * regmap_read/write on unready syscon MMIO during system idle.
+	 *
+	 * Return 0 (success) directly since __rpm_callback has no 'out'
+	 * label (only 'fail:'). The actual hardware state will be set up
+	 * later when the system is ready.
+	 */
+	if (!cix_system_ready && cb) {
+		spin_unlock_irq(&dev->power.lock);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (dev->power.irq_safe) {
 		spin_unlock(&dev->power.lock);
 	} else {
